From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: no_trace <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ghosthook: install RW ghost data with DBM write permission

Ghost data has no VMA and therefore has no COW fault path.  The private
VM_READ|VM_WRITE protection selected PAGE_COPY, which is initially read-only
on arm64; a Ghost-code STR consequently raised a permission abort.  Select
the shared writable page protection for this trusted, kernel-owned backing so
the installed leaf includes PTE_WRITE/DBM.  The external API remains limited
to a bounded code/data pair and the page is still inaccessible to ordinary
VMA operations.

---
 mm/gh_ghost.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/gh_ghost.c b/mm/gh_ghost.c
index d0b61c5197b1..8d8a28cecab1 100644
--- a/mm/gh_ghost.c
+++ b/mm/gh_ghost.c
@@ -216,7 +216,11 @@ int gh_ghost_region_create(struct mm_struct *mm, unsigned long user_addr,
 	ret = apply_to_page_range(mm, user_addr, length, gh_ghost_pte_callback, &txn);
 	if (ret)
 		goto fail_unlock;
-	txn.prot = vm_get_page_prot(VM_READ | VM_WRITE | VM_MAYREAD | VM_MAYWRITE);
+	/* Ghost backing has no VMA/COW fault path.  PAGE_COPY would install a
+	 * read-only PTE; use the trusted shared-RW leaf so EL0 Ghost code can
+	 * update its paired state through arm64 DBM. */
+	txn.prot = vm_get_page_prot(VM_READ | VM_WRITE | VM_MAYREAD |
+				    VM_MAYWRITE | VM_SHARED);
 	txn.op = GH_GHOST_PTE_INSTALL;
 	ret = apply_to_page_range(mm, user_addr, length,
 					 gh_ghost_pte_callback, &txn);
